## Uppercase base prefixes do not match the integer grammar: Sec 3.6
## defines hex/oct/bin with the lowercase literal prefixes "0x"/"0o"/"0b",
## and Sec 5.2 rule 13 matches numeric literals case-sensitively, so a
## body like 0X1A falls through to rule 15 and is a String carrying the
## body exactly as written. Lowercase-prefixed bodies in the same
## document are Integers; uppercase hex DIGITS after a lowercase prefix
## stay Integers too (hex_digit allows 0-9a-fA-F). A bare 0x with no
## digit after the prefix is not an integer either (hex requires at
## least one hex_digit), so it is a String as well.
bare_hex: 0X1A
bare_oct: 0O17
bare_bin: 0B101
neg_hex: -0XFF
plus_hex: +0XFF
bare_prefix_only: 0x
lower_hex: 0x1A
lower_oct: 0o17
lower_bin: 0b101
uppercase_digits_hex: 0xAB
mixed_digits_hex: 0xDEADbeef
